<h1 id="Introduction">Introduction<a class="anchor-link" href="#Introduction">¶</a></h1><p>Generalized Linear Models (GLM) with regularization are powerful tools for building predictive models while preventing overfitting. Regularization techniques such as Lasso (L1), Ridge (L2), and ElasticNet add penalty terms to the model to constrain coefficient estimates, improving generalization to new data.
In this assignment, we will train GLM models with each of these regularization methods and evaluate their performance using multiple key metrics — not just accuracy, but also Precision-Recall, ROC-AUC, Cumulative Lift, and F1 Score.
Finally, we will compare these GLM models with the performance of ensemble models (Random Forest, GBM, XGBoost, CatBoost) built in the previous assignment to determine the best model overall.</p>
